- `bun test` -> `358 pass / 0 fail`, EXIT 0 — STAYS GREEN (see Note below)
- Behavioral probe (audit-style 4-cycle loop with post-trip reads, same as
  pristine probe above) under this sabotage:
  `SABOTAGED pending=3` (2x `read: Recovered via read ...` + 1x edit),
  probe throws `RED AS EXPECTED: got 3 lessons instead of 1`, EXIT 1
  (RED confirmed at behavioral level — reproduces audit OH-6.7 symptom verbatim)
- Restore: `git checkout -- src/context/episodic-memory.ts` -> EXIT 0
- Post-restore `bun test -t "OH-6.7-lesson-per-read"` -> 1 pass, EXIT 0
- NOTE (test-coverage gap, carried to QA verdict): the shipped
  `OH-6.7-lesson-per-read` pipeline test performs its re-reads BEFORE the
  trip is established (read-ok, edit-fail, read-ok, edit-fail, then good edit),
  so the `=== "other"` carve-out is never exercised by the test and B1 does
  not fail the suite. The production fix itself is proven load-bearing by the
  audit-style probe (pristine 1 vs sabotaged 3). Recommend the programmer
  extend the pipeline test with post-trip re-reads before merge.

